Intermittent, timing-dependent failure only observed under the full concurrent test suite (not reproducible in isolation): z3-4.8.12 emits an undocumented diagnostic comment line (e.g. "; declare-sort-parameter line: 4 position: 25") on stdout immediately after an "unsupported" response to an unrecognized command, which jSMTLIB's response parser normally strips as a standard SMT-LIB ';' comment; under concurrent solver-process load a fragment of that comment line (e.g. the command name "declare-sort-parameter") occasionally leaks into the parsed response for the next command instead of being fully consumed with the first, producing a spurious mismatch against the golden -- the same solver-process stream-reading race also seen with z3-4.14.1 on ok_setOptionalOptions.tst, not a defect in the test or golden
